WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:03.897
Give an AI agent Blender and a real photo or video.

00:03.907 --> 00:05.736
Can it rebuild that scene in 3D?

00:06.036 --> 00:11.239
We introduce BlenderWorld: 223 real-world 3D creation tasks,

00:11.249 --> 00:14.880
spanning 9 categories and 16 application scenarios.

00:15.180 --> 00:19.566
Inputs can be text, images, videos, or attached specification files.

00:19.576 --> 00:24.799
In Blender, the agent codes, renders, and inspects, then delivers an editable project.

00:25.099 --> 00:27.847
Real requests rarely have a single right answer.

00:27.857 --> 00:32.746
So an evaluator agent first renders eight task-specific views of each submission.

00:32.756 --> 00:37.867
Then 2,651 binary rubric items check each requirement:

00:37.877 --> 00:42.477
a vision-language judge checks the renders; an agent judge inspects the scene file.

00:42.487 --> 00:44.657
Eight visual-quality scores are fused in.

00:44.957 --> 00:50.276
Across 13 frontier models, GPT-6-Astra leads with 79.9,

00:50.286 --> 00:54.978
yet it passes every rubric item on only 42.2% of tasks.

00:55.278 --> 00:57.399
More tool calls don't mean better work.

00:57.409 --> 01:01.214
From another angle, people vanish, characters float, details distort.

01:01.224 --> 01:04.367
True 3D spatial coherence is still the bottleneck.

01:04.667 --> 01:08.915
BlenderWorld: measuring how well AI brings the real world into 3D.
